      ],
      "summary": "RDF <-> property-graph mapping and SPARQL 1.1 compiled to GraphView scans, the pure-Rust SHACL Core and ShEx Core validators over eg-rdf's oxrdf model, and the native GraphQL read surface (schema-from-graph + a resolver compiling to GraphView scans). Grouped as one seam because all four share the oxrdf term/graph model and the GraphView scan contract. Carries an undocumented dev-dependency cycle (eg-rdf dev-depends eg-shacl, which depends on eg-rdf) -- see D-EG-003."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/epistemic-graph/registry/eg-server-dispatch",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "eg.server-dispatch",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/epistemic-graph",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/epistemic-graph/component-registry/eg-server-dispatch",
      "layer": "server-protocol",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "eg.server-protocol",
        "eg.kg-delegate",
        "eg.policy-aware-query-dispatch",
        "eg.wire-protocol-family",
        "eg.federation",
        "eg.cdc",
        "eg.blob-store",
        "eg.kv-surface",
        "eg.s3-surface",
        "eg.obda"
      ],
      "summary": "The root facade's server/protocol adapter and the TOP of the DAG. There is deliberately no eg-server crate: the server lib and the bin are 1:1, so splitting would carry no consumer and entangle the server/metrics features. Owns dispatch.rs (14,174 lines -- the 'thin routing table' convention describes the intent, not the present state), handlers/, state.rs, auth.rs, access.rs, transport.rs, mutation.rs, mutation_batch.rs, the ten-member wire family (pgwire, mysql_wire, mssql_wire, bolt_wire, redis_wire, sqlite_wire, amqp_wire, mqtt_wire, stomp_wire, broker_wire), federation/, cdc*, s3/, lake/, obda/, blob/ and kv.rs. It is the one permitted caller of IsolationLayer::mint_policy_decision_lease (authorize_and_route_knowledge_stream), enforced by the mint-lease-call-sites hook."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/epistemic-graph/registry/eg-server-protocol",
