    {
      "id": "component/epistemic-graph/registry/eg-viz",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "eg.viz",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/epistemic-graph",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/epistemic-graph/component-registry/eg-viz",
      "layer": "query-reasoning",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "eg.view-spec-contract",
        "eg.viz-columnstore",
        "eg.viz-lod-kernels",
        "eg.viz-graph-tiles",
        "eg.viz-export"
      ],
      "summary": "The native visualization stack. eg-viz-core is the declarative ViewSpec chart IR, the ViewResult exact-vs-approximated metadata, the mark capability matrix and the LOD tier-selection rules -- a true leaf with ZERO normal-build workspace dependencies. Above it: the columnstore, the M4/LTTB kernels (runtime-detected AVX2), graph tiles and export. CORRECTION to the skill: the viz features are NOT all off by default -- `full` (which is in `default`) enables viz, viz-columnstore, viz-static-export, viz-interactive and viz-graph-tiles."
    },
    {
      "id": "component/epistemic-graph/registry/eg-wire-contracts",
      "type": "Component",
      "label": "eg.wire-contracts",
      "partOfRepo": "repo/epistemic-graph",
      "documentedBy": "manpage/epistemic-graph/component-registry/eg-wire-contracts",
      "layer": "types",
      "status": "proposed",
      "capabilityIds": [
        "eg.contracts",
        "eg.mutation-batch-contract",
        "eg.method-policy-ledger",
        "eg.durable-execution-routing",
        "eg.host-resource-capacity",
        "eg.agent-library-entry"
      ],
      "summary": "The zero- and one-edge contract leaves every other component imports. eg-types is the BOTTOM of the DAG and the only crate the whole workspace can see: protocol.rs (Request/Response/Method/ResultPayload), types.rs, wire.rs, acl.rs and the MutationBatch v1 contract itself (mutation_batch/, incl. MutationScope, MutationScopeIdentity, PRIVATE_PAYLOAD_EVENT_TYPES, COMPILED_BATCH_INCARNATION and the three domain predicates). eg-capabilities is the machine-checked MethodPolicy projection of eg_types::protocol::Method (deps = eg-types only). eg-durable carries routing contracts only (CallShape/WorkShape/DurableBackendKind) with no journal, lease or 2PC. eg-resource is dependency-free cgroup-aware capacity resolution. Grouped as one seam because all four are contract-only, are consumed workspace-wide, and splitting them would produce exactly the tiny-facade pattern the layout contract forbids. ADDED 2026-09-12 (F5): the RF-020 Agent Library identity contract also lives here, still within the existing `crates/eg-types/src/` root -- `agent_library.rs` (`AgentLibraryEntry`, `AgentLibraryLifecycle`, the schema-versioned definition/tool-surface digest domains, currently v5), `agent_component.rs`, `agent_graph.rs`, and `agent_template.rs`. This was UNCLAIMED as recently as the 5523859a/2026-09-04 verification; see `capability_authority_model.previously_unclaimed_now_claimed` for the correction record."
    },
